    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Three changes**, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `checkDigit`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` property (readOnly, string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** \u2014 new standalone helper (mirroring `Locality`/`CheckDigit`) that turns `+61412345678` into `+61 412 345 678`: recognises the country code from the E.164 prefix (`+61`/`+1`, the codes this app accepts, per `OwnerTelephone`), then groups the national digits in threes. Returns the input unchanged if it's null or not `+` followed by digits.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone()))\")`.\n\nThe test creates an owner with `telephone: \"0412 345 678\"` and asserts `$.telephone` = `+61412345678` (raw E.164, unchanged) and `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678` (human-formatted) \u2014 both now pass.",
